<TEI xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0" xml:id="CH2b1559-en-18cfe757" type="transl"><teiHeader><fileDesc><titleStmt><title>Draft translation of 聲無哀樂論</title><editor role="translator">Christoph Harbsmeier</editor></titleStmt><publicationStmt><ab>published electronically as part of the TLS project at https://hxwd.org</ab><availability status="2"><ab>This work has been licensed for use in the TLS</ab></availability></publicationStmt><sourceDesc><bibl><title>Draft translation of 聲無哀樂論</title>Draft: Oxford, 1971</bibl><ab>Translation of <bibl corresp="#CH2b1559"><title xml:lang="och"/></bibl> into <lang xml:lang="en">English</lang>.</ab></sourceDesc></fileDesc><profileDesc><creation resp="#CH">Initially created: <date>2026-05-10T21:05:56.502+09:00</date> by CH</creation></profileDesc></teiHeader><text><body><div><head>Translated parts</head><p xml:id="CH2b1559-start"><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.59" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T00:22:36.701+09:00">So then: the Music says this; the Music says that,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.60" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T00:32:04.919+09:00">is there no more to it than bells and drums (and no more)? [Music is more than the bells and drums that express it.]</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.61" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T00:23:53.965+09:00">Grief speaks of this, Grief speaks of that,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.62" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T00:32:53.359+09:00">is there no more to it than wailing and weeping? [Grief is more than its expression in wailing and weeping!</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.63" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T00:36:28.282+09:00">Speaking along these lines</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.64" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T00:37:49.348+09:00">jade and silk are not the substance of ritual (and?) deference</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.65" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T00:44:26.518+09:00">song and dance performance is not the main point of mourning.</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.66" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T00:45:06.742+09:00">How is one to make all this plain?</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.67" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T00:46:22.444+09:00">So: different regions have different customs:</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.68" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T00:48:18.979+09:00">their chanting and wailing is not the same.</seg></p></div></body></text></TEI>